# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository whichever git makes the commit.
#
# Without this, the conversion lived only in Git for Windows' own configuration
# (core.autocrlf), so any other git on the machine -- a toolchain's bundled MSYS2 git, say --
# committed files exactly as Windows wrote them. One such commit turned every line of
# catalog/tcgplayer-groups.json into a changed line, which then conflicted with the nightly
# price job's one-line edit to the same file.
* text=auto

# Batch files misbehave with bare LF endings.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
